        <div slot="tab-5">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gar-text-primary mb-4">Troubleshooting</h3>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">PAM authentication fails</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Ensure the PAM service file exists:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'ls -la /etc/pam.d/garlock', comment: 'Check PAM service exists' },
                  { command: 'cat /etc/pam.d/garlock', comment: 'View PAM configuration' },
                ]}
              />
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mt-3">
                If missing, create <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">/etc/pam.d/garlock</code> with <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">auth required pam_unix.so</code>
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Keyboard grab fails</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Another application may have grabbed the keyboard:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'xdotool getactivewindow', comment: 'Check active window' },
                  { command: 'RUST_LOG=debug garlock 2>&1 | grep -i grab', comment: 'View grab attempts' },
                ]}
              />
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mt-3">
                garlock retries up to 100 times. If it still fails, check for modal dialogs or fullscreen apps.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Screenshot capture fails</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">This can happen with some compositors:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'RUST_LOG=debug garlock 2>&1 | grep -i screenshot', comment: 'Check for errors' },
                ]}
              />
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mt-3">
                garlock will use the fallback solid color. Set <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">fallback_color</code> in config if you want a different color.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Config not loading</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Verify config file syntax:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'cat ~/.config/garlock/config.toml | tomlq .', comment: 'Validate TOML' },
                  { command: 'garlock --debug lock 2>&1 | grep -i config', comment: 'Check config loading' },
                ]}
              />
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Locked out of system</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Use a TTY to access your system:</p>
              <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gar-text-secondary space-y-1 text-sm mt-3">
                <li>Press <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">Ctrl+Alt+F2</code> to switch to TTY2</li>
                <li>Log in with your username and password</li>
                <li>Kill garlock: <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">pkill -9 garlock</code></li>
                <li>Return to GUI: <code class="text-gar-accent-blue">Ctrl+Alt+F7</code> (or F1)</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Ring not centered on correct monitor</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">garlock uses the primary monitor. Set your primary:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'xrandr --query | grep primary', comment: 'Check current primary' },
                  { command: 'xrandr --output HDMI-1 --primary', comment: 'Set primary monitor' },
                ]}
              />
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Daemon not responding</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Check if the daemon is running:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'pgrep -x garlock', comment: 'Check daemon process' },
                  { command: 'ls -la $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/garlock.sock', comment: 'Check socket exists' },
                  { command: 'garlock shutdown && garlock daemon &', comment: 'Restart daemon' },
                ]}
              />
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Slow blur processing</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Reduce blur radius or disable blur:</p>
              <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gar-text-muted/20 mt-3">
                <pre class="bg-gar-bg-primary p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="text-sm text-gar-text-primary font-mono">{`[background]
blur_radius = 10.0    # Lower = faster
# blur_radius = 0     # Disable completely`}</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Password with special characters fails</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Check keyboard layout:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'setxkbmap -query', comment: 'Check current layout' },
                  { command: 'setxkbmap us', comment: 'Switch to US layout if needed' },
                ]}
              />
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mt-3">
                garlock uses xkbcommon for keyboard handling. Ensure your keyboard layout matches what you used to set your password.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/20">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-2">Debug mode</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary text-sm mb-3">Run with verbose logging to diagnose issues:</p>
              <MultiTerminal
                commands={[
                  { command: 'RUST_LOG=debug garlock', comment: 'Debug logging' },
                  { command: 'RUST_LOG=garlock=trace garlock', comment: 'Trace logging' },
                  { command: 'garlock --debug lock', comment: 'Debug flag' },
                ]}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </TabbedCard>

      <!-- Back link -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gar-text-muted/10">
        <Button href="/" variant="ghost">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18" />
          </svg>
          Back to home
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
